  "summary": "Allen Police Chief Steve Dye briefed the City Council on the department's ALPR program, which includes 34 stationary cameras (13 Flock, 21 Motorola) plus vehicle-mounted readers and data-sharing with private properties. Dye described policies on retention, sharing agreements with 1,500+ Flock and 3,000+ Motorola agencies, prohibited uses (including immigration enforcement), and reported at least 21 arrests aided by ALPRs in 2026.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Allen Police Department has sharing agreements for Flock Safety ALPRs with over 1,500 other agencies and sharing agreements for Motorola Solutions ALPRs with over 3,000 other agencies",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "We cannot use this for immigration enforcement, traffic enforcement, harassment, intimidation",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    },
    {
      "quote": "Data collected from Flock Safety cameras are retained for 30 days while information collected by Vigilant cameras is retained for 90 days",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    }
  ],
